to","Date":"2025-06-08T01:38:10Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",29,1],"Message":"","SHA":"a6d061af6fde179e7e22d51892b2d6092fc21210"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-06-07T01:21:46Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",29,1],"Message":"","SHA":"84f4005c5fb813a55396c0231203a5614be7e355"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-06-06T01:22:10Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",29,1],"Message":"","SHA":"5e8840985b4753e1c299417db5e823d45abf2c66"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-06-05T01:29:24Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",29,1],"Message":"","SHA":"dd7ef202dc903c60de0b85b3ceed483a0013d158"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-06-04T01:28:11Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",29,1],"Message":"","SHA":"f22633244f187e4cbdbd1480fa55021061a82d6a"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-06-03T01:29:56Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",29,1],"Message":"","SHA":"f96b567dceba0696d0b9b133c0494027aaf91723"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-06-02T16:06:56Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",29,1],"Message":"","SHA":"01afb3b0cd695943c21ec0adfee42846ae8a93cf"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-06-02T01:25:34Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",28,1],"Message":"","SHA":"38278c736d55d6602ce3437a32667567dc4a1d2a"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-06-01T01:45:01Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",28,1],"Message":"","SHA":"51e87e9bf0f381f59a46bb056a224a42056aa453"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-31T01:20:13Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",28,1],"Message":"","SHA":"85830528db13d7acfdc63328513dbc56c8620e29"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-30T01:20:09Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",28,1],"Message":"","SHA":"c253086a79ecd9c7f72601a6367a3ac9532c881d"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-29T19:30:26Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",28,1],"Message":"chore(build): add gitignore for build artifacts\n\nAdded comprehensive .gitignore rules to exclude Tauri/Rust build artifacts while preserving final executable bundles. This addresses repository cleanliness and prevents accidental commits of:\n- Intermediate build files in debug/release directories\n- Platform-specific build outputs (x86_64-pc-windows-msvc)\n- Temporary NSIS/MSI/AppImage packaging artifacts\n\nKey inclusions ensure retention of:\n- Final Windows executables (.exe)\n- Installer packages (.msi)\n- Linux AppImages\n\nThis aligns with Land's cross-platform distribution strategy through Tauri while maintaining VS Code-level installation experience. The structure supports multiple build targets and prevents repository bloat from Rust's incremental compilation artifacts.","SHA":"556627990c17c287bcd880c5ab431c992f5de211"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-29T15:45:21Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",27,1],"Message":"build(config): add optimized Cargo release profile configuration\n\n- Set `target-dir` to \"Target\" to centralize build artifacts\n- Configure release profile with maximum optimizations:\n  - LTO enabled for cross-crate optimizations\n  - Codegen units reduced to 1 for better optimization\n  - Panic strategy set to abort for smaller binaries\n  - Strip symbols and disable debug info in release builds\n- Enforce git VCS for new crate initialization\n\nThese changes align with Land's core performance objectives by:\n1. Reducing final binary size through stripping and panic abort\n2. Improving runtime performance via aggressive LTO and opt-level 3\n3. Establishing consistent build artifact management\n4. Ensuring clean project initialization practices\n\nParticularly critical for the Mountain (Rust backend) component where release build efficiency directly impacts application startup time and memory footprint versus Electron baseline.","SHA":"ebe581bae6972ee8ad05691507419aa9ddafb0f2"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-29T01:22:09Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"7e7ff60695e0910f2948d18bc658189af7190761"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-28T01:22:23Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"563a591324e3dc7bff1157d622916dfe549a0fc1"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-27T01:20:53Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"3f751a5051979fad9a4de111f40d1afb2d18c595"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-26T01:23:34Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"5e543b8783a881361515474a831e447b46c3fd87"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-25T01:36:15Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"16ad38fc67eeb46b179ccd6b58c0fdc11a78d9c3"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-24T01:18:55Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"84335e6842f49ac5264b2df27de472914690f7ba"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-23T09:43:24Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"Merge branch 'Current' of ssh://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Document into Current","SHA":"5b5c61b49464c0888754dc71d9c34a3dec07790c"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-23T09:43:22Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"8fedaa42b8c45cc50b46da4cac20c8ee79fabee6"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-23T01:21:32Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"72a25a7d14a4e1a8699fdb678b2b5b960c34e528"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-22T04:41:55Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"docs(LICENSE): Switch to CC0 1.0 Universal license\n\n- Replaces custom Land Public License (LPL v1.0) with CC0 public domain dedication\n- Removes copyleft requirements and complex license compatibility clauses from LPL\n- Aligns with Land project's goal of maximum openness by dedicating work to public domain\n- Simplifies third-party contributions by eliminating patent litigation clauses\n- Retains only CC0's warranty disclaimer and liability limitations\n- Requires no attribution, enabling unrestricted use/modification/distribution\n- Impacts all project components by removing previous LPL obligations while maintaining permissive access","SHA":"f1c2f5065cfd9a3bebab4cfa71fb9f2dd5434d45"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-22T01:21:25Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"2bf0b0896bda445f732a96e158553d80a42ecd29"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-21T01:22:18Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"519e3dd3d98b4141e94e12307e61b86ae0efc388"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-20T18:15:42Z","File":["⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,2],"Message":"docs(contributing): normalize code of conduct and contribution guideline links\n\n- Standardized URL casing in CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md and CONTRIBUTING.md from uppercase 'HTTPS' to lowercase 'https'\n- Maintains documentation consistency across project governance files\n- Improves markdown readability while preserving link functionality\n- Aligns with common documentation practices observed in open source projects, supporting Land's goal of fostering a collaborative community environment\n\nThis change demonstrates attention to detail in project documentation hygiene without affecting core editor functionality.","SHA":"cd478d1350f1524507280d7c50fba4de876510d4"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-20T01:22:39Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"da29de69be6a7a37a19b6a2d3196cb78958a1bb3"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-19T01:24:55Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"49d420f8c4fbc523d002b19356d787ea0e4ebc44"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-18T01:26:34Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"d7f0bdb7f3cb3824e4005366f2c278493095e093"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-17T01:19:46Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"d51e8e1ea17cef4d5132a83ed342b14cc4482606"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-16T01:21:53Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"84568cfd88deffff7ff9866aca546dbc5cee8a6c"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-15T01:18:47Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"1192397f5ed00458dbd5b312c4d0abe25c83662b"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-14T01:20:38Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"93091f7b2a473015e30968ceeabe9e2fdf6f6c5a"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-13T01:21:55Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"4af47bf1cbd696ba856a8194ca454f206bc6f7d5"},{"Author":"github-actions[bot]","Date":"2025-05-12T07:30:50Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"Merge pull request #33 from CodeEditorLand/dependabot/github_actions/dependabot/fetch-metadata-2.4.0\n\nBump dependabot/fetch-metadata from 2.3.0 to 2.4.0","SHA":"4c4a4e0a8e3a7d8ba4e2e56d8127300f0aead47d"},{"Author":"dependabot[bot]","Date":"2025-05-12T07:30:38Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"Bump dependabot/fetch-metadata from 2.3.0 to 2.4.0\n\nBumps [dependabot/fetch-metadata](https://github.com/dependabot/fetch-metadata) from 2.3.0 to 2.4.0.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/dependabot/fetch-metadata/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/dependabot/fetch-metadata/compare/v2.3.0...v2.4.0)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: dependabot/fetch-metadata\n  dependency-version: 2.4.0\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>","SHA":"86beaddc65bd2df4a16ec804429bae358f0a05a5"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-12T01:23:27Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"1a491d55667a6923129319f5d42bfc15bc2892f5"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-11T01:25:33Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"1691c0f6d20a1acf3a434fcec69292aca8b4745c"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-10T14:32:54Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"docs(LICENSE): Migrate from CC0 to Land Public License v1.0\n\nReplaced Creative Commons Zero license with custom Land Public License (LPL) v1.0 to establish clear copyleft terms for the Land project. Key changes:\n- Introduces strong copyleft provisions requiring LPL-licensed components to remain open\n- Defines compatibility rules for combining with External Works while maintaining LPL governance\n- Adds patent grants with defensive termination clauses\n- Implements attribution requirements and source code distribution obligations\n- Establishes Sofia, Bulgaria as jurisdiction for dispute resolution\n\nThis aligns with Land's goals to foster open collaboration while protecting against proprietary forks. The LPL ensures contributions remain freely available under reciprocal terms, supporting sustainable ecosystem growth around the Tauri-based editor architecture.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: Transition from permissive CC0 to copyleft LPL v1.0 significantly alters distribution rights. All future contributions must be licensed under LPL terms.","SHA":"820365a35ba5be50b24f86b156536ba2fda19c17"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-10T01:17:59Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"0708bd8680cf9835d4f1046255bc5dcb1f6b107a"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-09T01:20:29Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"6e8b9611703606bc1839ffd766153bc7079f85d4"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-08T01:21:07Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"4142df87010ca7b345dec42feb1a95b6c574a159"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-07T01:20:38Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"ff9870e2df5ee9aecacd35d8c5aa9c66c1da3dc9"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-06T01:20:17Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"f2b09f2f681e105ee9f55373740530d5bde44151"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2025-05-05T04:05:27Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"a5ac1486c1a639f13aeff73a2e03fa80e4b6db80"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-05T01:22:57Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"3799070e115cf07afbf298594af47b50f3fb0798"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-04T01:26:57Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"93777732536768a4a76f34db71c9447b8a1474a6"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-03T01:17:55Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"799112abaea08b4308ca4c2e0290b4955658b6c4"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-02T01:19:41Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"23b1d23a3c04c9e9fa4043872efc08cb02a50061"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-05-01T01:26:08Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"d1f3b0b3d3660ad422119dab253df27d20e4935c"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-04-30T01:19:21Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"95ecb0911ca39e74fc5e0bf45c6cb04832619a6d"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-04-29T01:19:09Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"637a6dc4b378072b6a4301f23a129ec29e6792ac"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-04-28T01:21:04Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",25,1],"Message":"","SHA":"8fa27c6a5931f30b17de7d7e6403a6fd9e8157b6"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2025-04-27T01:23:26Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",2